

# ⚽ AI Football Intelligence System

### 🚀 ScaleDown Challenge Project

An end-to-end Machine Learning system that predicts **Expected Goals (xG)** — the probability of a shot resulting in a goal — using real football match data.

Built as part of the **ScaleDown Challenge**, this project focuses on delivering an optimized, efficient, and deployable AI solution for sports analytics.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

In football analytics, goals alone do not fully represent performance.
The **Expected Goals (xG)** metric helps evaluate the quality of scoring chances.

This system:

* Uses real StatsBomb CSV shot data
* Engineers spatial features like shot distance and angle
* Trains a Logistic Regression model
* Evaluates performance using ROC-AUC and Accuracy
* Deploys predictions via a Streamlit web application

---

## 🧠 ScaleDown Challenge Focus

The ScaleDown Challenge emphasizes building impactful systems with optimized complexity.

This project achieves that by:

* Using lightweight and interpretable models
* Reducing unnecessary feature complexity
* Ensuring fast training and inference
* Deploying an efficient interactive interface

The result is a scalable and production-ready football analytics system.

---

## 📊 Dataset

The model is trained using **StatsBomb shot event CSV data**.

Features include:

* Shot location (X, Y coordinates)
* Shot distance from goal
* Shot angle
* Shot outcome (Goal / No Goal)

The dataset enables realistic and practical xG predictions.

---

## ⚙️ System Architecture

### 1️⃣ Data Processing

* Load CSV dataset
* Clean and preprocess shot data
* Encode target variable

### 2️⃣ Feature Engineering

* Calculate shot distance
* Compute shot angle
* Prepare model-ready feature set

### 3️⃣ Model Training

* Algorithm: Logistic Regression
* Binary classification (Goal vs No Goal)

### 4️⃣ Model Evaluation

* Accuracy Score
* ROC-AUC Score
* Confusion Matrix

### 5️⃣ Deployment

* Built with Streamlit
* Interactive user interface
* Real-time xG prediction

---

## 💻 Tech Stack

* Python
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Scikit-learn
* Matplotlib
* Streamlit

---

## 🚀 Installation & Setup

### Clone the Repository

```
git clone https://github.com/mrmysterious27/AI-Football-Intelligence-System.git
cd AI-Football-Intelligence-System
```

### Install Dependencies

```
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Run the Application

```
streamlit run app.py
```

